    "confidence": "high",
    "uncertainCells": [],
    "notes": "ORIGINAL PRINTING: the red-ink, typewriter-style, one-sided 1960 Virdon card (left-hand card of the 1600x1402 scan; the right-hand card is the modern-typeface reissue transcribed as batter_virdon-bill_1960). It differs from the modern printing in its ratings (stealing-B here, stealing-C on the modern card) and in a completely different grid arrangement with the same statistics box: e.g. this card prints HOMERUN at col3 r2 and HOMERUN 1-5 / DOUBLE 6-20 at col3 r3, where the modern card prints HOMERUN 1-7 / TRIPLE 8-20 at col2 r9, and it has three WALKs at col2 r10-12. Source: a 2019 collector's post of his Bill Virdon Strat-O-Matic cards (Wayback capture). Read from 1.1x half-card crops, then a second independent pass over a 1.0x crop of the whole grid. Roll numbers print with an en dash ('2–groundball'); 'outs as pos- sible' is line-wrap hyphenation, recorded as 'into as many outs as possible'. Col1 roll12 prints 'plus injury' under 'flyball (rf)B'. 1960 BATTING RECORD box lists the seven stats AT BATS, DOUBLES, TRIPLES, HOMERUNS, AVERAGE, WALKS, STRIKEOUTS."
  }
